omputer skills. Concerns: pretentious, sometimes adopts wrong tone when communicating. So crew cooperation and professional communication concerns.\n\nCandidate C strengths: can make correct decisions quickly, excellent attention skills, puts concern for others above everything. Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not very willing to further his education. So communication issues, adaptability.\n\nCandidate D strengths: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Concerns: considered moody, regarded as a loner. So crew cooperation issues, mood stability.\n\nCandidate A strengths: anticipate dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities. Concerns: unfriendly, eats unhealthily, not good at taking criticism, can be unorganized.\n\nWe need to weigh. Stress resilience is crucial; B has explicit evidence. A unknown. C unknown. D unknown. So B currently strongest on stress. But B has communication tone issues. C has communication difficulty but also puts concern for others above everything (crew cooperation). D is moody and loner, which may affect crew cooperation.\n\nThus B seems best overall, but we need to consider crew cooperation. B is pretentious and sometimes wrong tone, which could affect crew. C's concern for others may offset communication difficulty? But egocentric and not willing to further education are concerns.\n\nWe could ask for more info on Candidate C's communication style or teamwork, but we need to give a vote now. Perhaps we can vote for Candidate B, but note we need to discuss C and D further. Or we could propose Candidate C as a strong alternative due to decision quality and crew concern for others, but communication issues may be mitigated.\n\nGiven the current discussion, Agent 2 shifted to B. I could either agree, or challenge, bringing up C. I think we should bring up Candidate C as a strong alternative, highlighting his decision speed, attention, and concern for others, while noting communication difficulty and egocentric. Compare to B's pretentiousness. I could argue that C's concern for others may outweigh B's pretentiousness, and that decision quality is critical. However, C's lack of willingness to further education is a concern for adaptability.\n\nWe need to state a vote. Perhaps we can vote for Candidate B, but note that we need to discuss C and D before final. Or we could vote for Candidate C as a balanced candidate. Which is more plausible? The panel hasn't discussed C yet, so bringing it up is good. But we must give a vote now. The instruction says each turn must include a vote. So we can vote for B, but we can also say we think B is currently strongest, but we need to explore C and D.\n\nThus: \"I agree with Agent 2 that B is currently the strongest, given stress handling and conscientiousness, but we still need to evaluate C and D. I vote for Candidate B.\"\n\nWe need to reference explicit facts: B handles stress very well, very conscientious, good at assessing weather conditions. Concern: pretentious, wrong tone. Compare to A's unknown stress and unfriendly. So B is better.\n\nThus produce public message and metadata JSON with vote \"Candidate B\"."}
